body:
Yes this is a bug in the `package.json` for linqts. See https://unpkg.com/linqts@1.12.5/package.json

```
{
  "name": "linqts",
  "version": "1.12.5",
  "description": "LinQ + TypeScript",
  "es2015": "index.ts",
  "source": "index.ts",
  ...
```

The `es2015` property should not point to the non-existing `index.ts` file.

You can work around this by placing the following `ngcc.config.js` file at the root of your project:

```
module.exports = {
  packages: {
    'linqts': {
      entryPoints: {
        '.': {
          override: { es2015: undefined }
        }
      }
    }
  }
};
```

This should tell ngcc to ignore this property in the `package.json`.

Actually I just realised that `linqts` does not contain any Angular, does it? In which case we could just tell ngcc to ignore it:

```
module.exports = {
  packages: {
    'linqts': {
      entryPoints: {
        '.': {
          ignore: true
        }
      }
    }
  }
};
```

That being said, it should already be ignored by ngcc as it has no `...metadata.json` file, so I am not sure why it is erroring in the first place.

I tried:

```
mkdir temp
cd temp
yarn init
yarn add linqts
yarn add @angular/compiler
yarn add @angular/compiler-cli
yarn add typescript
yarn ivy-ngcc -l debug
```

which runs fine:

```
Compiling @angular/compiler/testing : fesm2015 as esm2015
Compiling @angular/compiler/testing : fesm5 as esm5
Compiling @angular/compiler/testing : esm2015 as esm2015
Compiling @angular/compiler/testing : esm5 as esm5
Compiling @angular/compiler/testing : main as umd
```
